  "configuration_id": "config_008",
  "reason": "Evidence: config_002 (multimodal, multiprofile, scgpt, resnet50, avgpool, concat) is the best at 0.5121, far exceeding config_051 (multimodal, singleprofile) at 0.4275, confirming multiprofile is a major driver. However, the multimodal-vs-rna_only gap at singleprofile is only ~1.7% (config_051 vs config_018), which is weak and possibly noise. We have no multiprofile rna_only baseline to determine whether the image modality is actually contributing at the multiprofile level. Question: config_008 (rna_only, multiprofile, scgpt, avgpool) is a clean single-variable ablation of config_002—removing only the image modality. If it performs near 0.51, the image adds little and we can simplify; if it drops substantially, the image is essential and we should invest in image-encoder choices (e.g., ViT-L). Why this is best: under a limited budget, resolving whether the image modality is a meaningful contributor is the highest-value uncertainty to reduce before committing further experiments to image-encoder or fusion variations. It also guards against over-investing in a more complex multimodal pipeline if a simpler rna_only multiprofile model is competitive."
}

